---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { api, repository, workbench } from '../lib/links';
import { sitePath } from '../lib/site-path';
import snippet from '../examples/first-model.ts?raw';
import SourceCode from '../components/SourceCode.astro';
---
<Layout title="Start with the model — Foldkit Zloz">
  <section class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Developer guide / Local preview</p><h1>Start with the model.</h1><p>Keep your graph, architecture semantics and changes explicit. Compose a view when you need one.</p></section>
  <section class="guide-section"><div><h2>Use the existing packages.</h2><p>Zloz is the product name. This checkout still uses the technical package names below; package naming and publication are separate release work.</p><p>Run <code>bun install --frozen-lockfile</code> from the repository root, then <code>bun run dev:flow-sample</code> for the board or <code>bun run dev:zloz-promo</code> for this site. The board dev port is 4327; the reviewed preview link is separately configurable.</p><a class="text-link" href={repository}>Open the repository ↗</a></div><dl class="package-map"><dt>@opsydyn/foldkit-flow</dt><dd>Graph model, immutable editor, geometry and C4 / DDD semantics.</dd><dt>@opsydyn/foldkit-flow/foldkit</dt><dd>Optional native Foldkit views, policies, composable renderers and theme tokens.</dd><dt>@opsydyn/foldkit-flow-elk / -force</dt><dd>Optional layout adapters, separate from the graph core.</dd><dt>@opsydyn/foldkit-flow-mermaid</dt><dd>Mermaid export with identity mapping and conversion-loss reporting.</dd></dl></section>
  <section class="guide-section"><div><h2>Meaning first.<br />Rendering second.</h2><p>This example uses the actual public core contract. The core has no browser or renderer dependency. The optional Foldkit adapter keeps interaction in Model → view → Message → update.</p><a class="text-link" href={api}>Browse the API and type contracts ↗</a></div><div class="code-panel"><SourceCode code={snippet} lang="ts" sourceId="first-model.ts" /></div></section>
  <section class="guide-section"><div><h2>Your visual language.</h2><p>Compose custom node bodies, edge labels, controls and layouts. Apply scoped theme tokens through <code>FlowTheme</code>; keep application styling outside the headless graph model.</p><a class="text-link" href={workbench}>Open the workbench ↗</a></div><div><h2>Portable, with honest losses.</h2><p>Canonical JSON preserves the model. Mermaid carries diagram source plus a separate identity map and reports what cannot survive conversion, including layout and richer semantic details.</p><div class="download-links"><a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/downloads/order-context.json')} download>Canonical JSON ↓</a><a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/downloads/order-context.mermaid.json')} download>Mermaid bundle ↓</a></div></div></section>
</Layout>
